  "reading": {
   "title": "Hafsa's morning",
   "text": "Hafsa gets up at six o'clock every morning. First, she takes a shower and brushes her teeth. Then she makes tea and breakfast. She usually eats bread, cheese and olives.\n\nHer son Emre wakes up at seven. He takes a shower, and he gets dressed for school. He drinks a glass of milk and eats his breakfast fast. At seven forty, he takes the bus to school.\n\nAfter Emre leaves, Hafsa washes the dishes. Her neighbor Linda calls her every morning. They talk about the weather and the news. Sometimes Linda laughs and says, \"Hafsa, you work too hard!\" Hafsa smiles and drinks more tea. At nine o'clock, Hafsa studies English for one hour. She loves her morning routine because the house is quiet and peaceful.",
